			"Message": "chore(Mountain): Sync submodule to centralize Cocoon IPC and URI sanitization\n\nUpdate the Mountain submodule to revision a430e1c4 to continue the standardization of the native backend IPC layer.\n\n**Key Changes:**\n- Introduce the `proxy_cocoon` helper in `Utilities::Proxy` to replace verbose inline `SendRequestToSideCar` logic in `CustomEditorProvider`, `StatusBarProvider`, `TestProvider`, `Authentication`, `Task`, and `FileSystem` handlers. This abstracts `ApplicationRunTime` retrieval and method string construction.\n- Consolidate URI sanitization by extracting `StripFileUriScheme` into `Utilities::Params` as `strip_file_uri`. Apply this to all `FileSystem` operations (ReadFile, WriteFile, Stat, etc.) to normalize `file://` URI variants consistently.\n\nThese changes reduce boilerplate in the extension host communication layer and ensure robust, unified path handling across the IPC surface.",
			"SHA": "6b92b99db0ac3e58b59bba147bba049ec482773e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T11:02:04Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Mountain): Sync submodule to centralize URI sanitization and unify IPC dispatch\n\nUpdate the Mountain submodule to revision 4887af8a to continue the standardization of the native backend IPC layer.\n\n**Key Changes:**\n- Extend the `call!` macro in `WindServiceHandlers` with a new overload for handlers accepting no arguments, eliminating repetitive boilerplate across Extensions, Decorations, WorkingCopy, Keybinding, and Lifecycle dispatchers.\n- Centralize URI sanitization logic by extracting `StripFileUriScheme` from `FileReadAlias.rs` into `Utilities::Params` as `strip_file_uri`. This unifies the handling of `file://`, `file:///`, and `file://localhost` forms across the request tracking layer.\n\nThese changes reduce code duplication in the IPC dispatcher and ensure consistent path normalization for file system operations, aligning with the project's Effect-based architectural principles.",
			"SHA": "31f4058cfeb7c7e0a90cd209e1777fdb0db2bc6d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T11:00:10Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Sync Mountain submodule for IPC handler standardization\n\nSynchronize the Mountain submodule to revision aef9a349 to introduce centralized macro utilities and parameter helpers for the native backend IPC layer.\n\n**Mountain:** Implement the `effect!` macro within `MappedEffectType` to streamline the conversion of async logic into `MappedEffect` closures. Introduce the `Utilities::Params` module to provide type-safe, default-aware argument extractors (e.g., `string_at`, `u64_at`) for `serde_json::Value` payloads. Apply these utilities across the entire `Track/Effect/CreateEffectForRequest` tree, covering `Authentication`, `FileSystem`, `Terminal`, `WindowUI`, and `Workspace` handlers. Additionally, refactor `WindServiceHandlers/mod.rs` to adopt the new `call!` macro, unifying dispatch logic and logging for Tauri IPC commands.\n\nThese changes eliminate repetitive boilerplate, enforce consistent parameter extraction patterns, and align the Mountain backend with the project's Effect-based architectural principles.",
			"SHA": "05ecea8bfce4d72622df9c859f465ad6a2401775"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T10:44:29Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Adopt standardized argument helpers in FileSystem and Git handlers\n\nApply the `JsonValueHelpers` utility module to the `FileSystem` and `Git` IPC handler namespaces to enforce consistent argument extraction patterns.\n\nReplace verbose `Arguments.get(...).and_then(...).unwrap_or(...)` chains with type-safe helper functions (`arg_string`, `arg_u64`, `arg_bool_true`) across `FileMkdir`, `FileCloseFd`, and `HandleExec` handlers. This unifies the codebase with the broader refactoring initiated in recent commits, reducing boilerplate and ensuring robust default value handling for the native backend IPC surface.",
			"SHA": "086cbf480dea4dbbc1bc855b2fef60e3a282cb2a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T10:42:34Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Standardize Wind service argument extraction\n\nIntroduce a centralized `JsonValueHelpers` utility module to provide type-safe, default-aware argument extraction functions (`arg_string`, `arg_u64`, `arg_bool`, etc.). Replace ad-hoc `Arguments.get(n).and_then(...).unwrap_or(...)` patterns scattered across 40+ IPC handler modules with calls to these standardized helpers.\n\nThis refactoring affects the entire `WindServiceHandlers` tree, covering Cocoon, Git, Terminal, UI, and NativeHost namespaces. The `mod.rs` exports are updated, and the main `mountain_ipc_invoke` dispatcher is refactored to utilize the new utilities for command routing. This reduces boilerplate, ensures consistent default value handling, and improves type safety across the Mountain backend's IPC surface.",
			"SHA": "ec2fef2c499f821bc845ede09490763da058b0f0"
		}
	],
